# ci/scripts/perl_tests.sh holds an append-only list of test filenames in its
# working_tests array. Every security and bug-fix branch adds its own entry, so
# a normal three-way merge conflicts on almost every branch: 12 open branches
# touch this one file as of August 2026, and the OMK-12644 hardening epic has
# roughly another nine tickets still to land. `merge=union` keeps the added
# lines from both sides instead of raising a conflict.
#
# Caveat, so nobody is surprised later: union does not understand the file, it
# just keeps both sides. Two branches appending different tests is the case this
# is for, and it resolves correctly. Two branches editing the SAME line (renaming
# a test, say) leaves both versions in the array, and the stale filename then
# fails the build loudly rather than passing silently: `prove` errors on the
# missing file, the script records it and exits non-zero with the name in its
# FAILED summary (OMK-12829). Note this no longer aborts the run at the stale
# entry, so the rest of the suite still reports. test/t_ci_perl_tests.t pins
# both halves of that. A duplicated entry merely runs one test twice. Both are
# acceptable because the array contains nothing but filenames. Do not extend
# union to files where keeping both sides could be silently wrong.
ci/scripts/perl_tests.sh merge=union
